# Cursor Rules for this workspace

## Project layout
- Angular app (legacy): `src/app` at repo root. Dev server via `npm run start` (Angular CLI). Firebase compat was used; avoid changing it now.
- Next.js app (current): `next-portfolio/` with App Router, Tailwind v3, shadcn/ui (New York), Firebase (Firestore + Storage). Primary target for new work.

## Primary stack (next-portfolio)
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v3
- shadcn/ui (style: New York). Use components via `@/components/ui/*`.
- Firebase modular SDK: Firestore + Storage
- Static export enabled for GitHub Pages (`output: 'export'`), `images.unoptimized: true`

## Data model (Firestore + Storage)
- Use Firestore collections only (no Storage JSON fallback):
  - `profiles` (1 doc): { avatar: string (Storage path), name: string, title: string, presentation: string[], googleMap: string }
  - `languages`, `techSkills`: { title: string, value: string }
  - `educations`, `experiences`: { title: string, timeline: string, description: string }
  - `projects`: { category: string, image: string (Storage path), title: string, url: string }
- Resolve Storage paths with `getDownloadURL(ref(storage, path))` before rendering images.

## Environment
- All Firebase config comes from `.env.local` in `next-portfolio/`:
  - `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID`,
    `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID`
- For GitHub Pages builds, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/repo-name` before `npm run build`.

## Conventions
- Use client components only when necessary (e.g., when using `onSnapshot`, hooks, or interactive UI).
- Prefer Firestore realtime (`onSnapshot`) for About/Resume/Portfolio; keep server components thin.
- DO NOT reintroduce Storage JSON content (e.g., `content/*.json`).
- DO NOT use `legacyBehavior` on `next/link`. Use shadcn `NavigationMenuLink` with `asChild` to wrap `Link` when needed.
- Keep Tailwind v3; avoid Tailwind v4 syntax.
- Use `@/` import alias (see `tsconfig.json`).
- Maintain static export compatibility: avoid features requiring Node APIs at runtime.

## Code style
- Strongly typed public APIs; avoid `any`.
- Clear, descriptive names; early returns; minimal nesting.
- Keep components small and focused; extract UI into `src/components/*`.
- Follow shadcn style for UI primitives; do not modify generated UI files unnecessarily.

## Linting & build
- Ensure no ESLint warnings (e.g., no unused imports, no `legacyBehavior`).
- After edits in `next-portfolio/`, run `npm run build` to validate static export.
- If Windows EPERM on `.next`, stop dev server and remove `.next` before building.

## Common commands (from next-portfolio/)
- Dev: `npm run dev`
- Build (export): `npm run build` (outputs `out/`)

## Deployment
- GitHub Pages: publish `out/`. If repo is not `username.github.io`, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/repo-name` before build.
- Firebase Hosting SSR is optional; remove `output: 'export'` only if enabling SSR.

## Do / Don’t
- DO: Use Firestore collections described above; resolve Storage paths for images.
- DO: Use shadcn components for UI; Tailwind for layout/spacing.
- DO: Keep Contact page backed by Firestore (`profiles.googleMap`) when implemented.
- DON’T: Add or rely on `content/*.json` in Storage.
- DON’T: Use `legacyBehavior` on links or Tailwind v4 features.

## Open tasks (high-level)
- Contact page: add contact form (Firebase Function integration).
- SEO/meta per page, GH Pages CI workflow, tests/Lighthouse.